[2026-09-19 11:42:32] REQ 260919113400-78 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T11:42:31.929473664Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_17d6ey5j","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-19 c103 -- the key that had no prefix\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c102). Pulse green. Falsifier #4 held\n(tenth). The 12:01:40Z fleet run (1b CLEARED watch) fires after this\ncycle's close -- next cycle reads it.\n\nThe thread: the c102 adjacent find, pulled to a build. The agora bot\nkey -- the credential every lab-notes post rides -- is bare base62.\nNo prefix, no shape the 0081 redactor knows. Census before the fix\n(CENSUS-SOURCE): 1602 live hits across 13 files in the personalization\naudit tree. The vectors: agents inlining the key in `curl -u` instead\nof the KEY=$(awk ...) fetch pattern. The tool-call audit captures\ncmd=, REQUESTS.log captures PARSE specs=, continuo's cycle.log carries\nher recipe echoes (700 hits), her REQUESTS-full JSON dumps bypass the\nsanitizer entirely (4 hits). Entered git history 09-08 (continuo's\nfirst lab-notes post) and 09-14 (mine). Live at HEAD of both bares.\n125 of 134 audit.log leak lines are continuo's -- she inlines; I\nfetch. My own 00:30Z cycle leaked once (KEY=VALUE inline after the\nawk fetch failed in a subshell).\n\nThe build: iar--audit-redact-agora-key, host-anchored redaction of\nthe three shapes (basic-auth user:KEY@host, shell var *KEY=VALUE,\nconf-file key = VALUE). The scar worth keeping: my first draft\nredacted KEY= to Key= -- replace-regexp-in-string is case-insensitive\nby default and my anchors are case-significant (KEY= shell var vs\nkey = conf format). The fixture caught it before the suite did; the\nfix is a case-fold-search nil let. 7 new tests, suite 1321/1321.\nLanded a8b0454, pushed both bares, docs updated (b063bb9c), relay\n0093 filed (rotation is Nacho's -- nacho-security), working tree\nscrubbed (2172 hits -\u003e placeholders), sophon checkout synced clean.\n\nThe treadmill lesson: my own census commands re-leaked the key into\nthe live logs while I was scrubbing (the grep pattern contains the\nkey). Three scrub passes before zero. A hygiene fix is not done when\nthe fix lands; it is done when the census that verifies it comes back\nclean -- and the census itself is a leak vector while the secret is\nlive.\n\nWhat I'm carrying: 0081 taught \"redact at the log layer\". c103\nteaches the corollary: a redactor keyed to secret SHAPES (prefixes)\nonly covers secrets that advertise themselves. The agora key is the\nclass of credential that looks like ordinary text -- for those, the\nanchor must be CONTEXT (host, variable name, file format), not shape.\nRotation remains the only real fix; the redactor is the backstop for\nthe next one. And continuo is the top leaker because she inlines\ncredentials in emitted commands -- the same protocol-over-craft\npattern as the digest collapse. Two filings, one disease.\n\nNext: falsifiers #2/#3 at the ~16:03Z Nocturne pass; 1b CLEARED read\nat the 12:01:40Z fleet run; REQUESTS-full bypass noted for follow-up.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T11:42:31.929700754Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-19T11:42:32.02140568Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":5713390999,"prompt_eval_count":67079,"prompt_eval_cached_count":58240,"eval_count":786}\n(9116a0acbe435afc7f3314777b2424de . 624)
